  "instance_name": "physical_ability_metaphor",
  "label": "Physical Ability as Metaphor for Support",
  "description": "The phrase 'stand by you' is a metaphor for emotional or physical support. The meme uses the literal inability to stand (due to disability) to contrast with the metaphorical meaning, implying that physical ability is a prerequisite for meaningful support — a concept that is not universally true and can be seen as reductive.",
